nn and williams ed  oliver you know nick bosa i think those  are the three guys that would be  worthy candidates for th where people in  the top 15 might go ooh this guy if i  can get this guy on my defense he can  change me around so now let's go to that  list there mike i mean to me that goes  down to maybe the buffalo bills would be  in that conversation you know with the  green bay packers okay maybe they want a  difference maker in their front seven  you talked about they have multiple  draft picks maybe that maybe they look  at it and go oh are we going to ed  oliver or quinn and williams or somehow  nick boses on the board at four maybe  they make a move something like that but  i think it's a very unique new  unique year sorry because of the  quarterback situation and nobody values  all any of those guys really as top two  or top three picks  and then the high-end talent maybe is  lacking in this draft a little bit as  compared to other drafts so uh that's  that's where i see it i don't know if  you guys think i missed anybody else  you'd certainly let me know and tell me  i'm wrong  no i i think that that makes a lot of  sense and it can go in a lot of  different directions you can see a lot  of different opportunities and and one  thing that is implicit in trading up  trading up from out of round one into  round one we've seen that happen over  and over again where teams will come up  back into round one after already using  a pick in the first round getting back  in and picking a quarterback late in the  process like the ravens did last year  when they got lamar jackson number 32.  remember there's value in being that  team that holds one of the low picks in  round one you get the guy for five years  it's better to get a guy at 30 31 32  than at the top of round two because you  control his rights for that fifth season  and the players for the most part don't  realize that they just think that it's  better to be a first-round pick than a  second-round pick not necessarily  if you're low enough in round one it's  better to go  top around two than bottom around once  so i would watch that too i think that's  where you're right that possibility for  that fifth quarterback comes in somebody  loving a guy and deciding we want to get  him bottom of round one and have him for  five years yeah i think i think that is  certainly the things to look out for  towards you know the end of the first  round you're right if daniel jones is  still on the board something like that  does somebody make a move whoever it may  be if one of the other quarterbacks fell  but again it is a unique unique year  without the top-tier top-shelf freaky  athletes okay there's a lot of good ones  in this but i really think i mentioned  the names that i think are you know  trade up into the top five and  specifically we're talking about the  jets at number three that list is short  for me it goes kyler murray ed oliver  quinn and williams nick bosa and it's  gonna be hopefully i think for the jets  in their best case scenario mike it  would be like okay  quinn and williams is on the board there  at number three  and a team gets scared that okay the  oakland raiders are gonna take quinn and  williams at number four so maybe the  buffalo bills decide to jump the raiders  at four and get to three those are the  possibilities i look at what if the  49ers take quinn and williams at two and  now nick bose is on the board at three  does that change the dynamic and now  another team goes oh wow i don't want to  leave him on the board for the oakland  raiders same type of thing but i think  that's where the jets come trade day  come draft night that's when it might  happen  and just because your trade up doesn't  mean it's guaranteed to work out last  year the saints went from 27 to 14. they  gave up the 27 pick last year and a  first round pick this year plus a fifth  round pick to get to marcus davenport  and so far davenport has not been nearly  as disrupti